WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.920
Here is a quick and easy full needle
rib cast on that's just two rows.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Now, before you try this, be sure you
understand racking on your machine.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.400
Review this video if you need help.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:25.080
The instructions for this cast
on start with rack H or swing H.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.360
Pull up a few needles and confirm
that your ribber is set to half pitch.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.760
The needles should be aligned like this.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.040
Now, because we'll be creating stitches
on all needles, be sure to use a yarn

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.720
that is finer than you
might normally knit ribbing.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.120
Set both beds for plain knitting.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.040
No tuck or slip buttons
or levers are engaged.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.840
Set both carriages to the main tension
for your garment or slightly tighter.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.640
Start by creating a zigzag row
by knitting from right to left.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.400
Hang the cast-on comb,

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.400
aligning it to the center and taking
care not to split any stitches.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.680
Hang weights as needed.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.360
Swing your ribber to the right
so that the needles are aligned like this.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.480
No matter what machine you're using,

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.280
make sure that the needles are
not crashing into each other.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.720
Notice that the stitches
are skewed to the right.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.880
Knit one row to the right.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.480
Now, rack back to the left, and

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.040
your needles should now be
in the original position.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.640
Again, half pitch,
and they're not crashing into each other.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.120
And continue knitting.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.000
Using the wire weight hangers can help.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.920
The cast-on is complete, and this is
called a full needle rib racked cast-on.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.280
This is a really fast cast-on,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:06.240
but it's fairly loose, and the cast-on
comb can distort that first row.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.600
Don't try and tighten the first
two rows of this cast-on.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.720
The stitches need to be loose
or large enough to rack.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.800
Consider casting on with waste yarn.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.400
Knit a few rows and then
knit one row of ravel cord.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.120
Thread up the carriage with the main

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:29.360
garment yarn and repeat that racked
cast on over that ravel cord.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.320
When you're done with your piece,
you can remove the ravel cord and you've

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.400
protected that cast on edge
from the cast on comb.

